# Commit messages

Canonical detail: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) **PR expectations** and [`docs/contributor-guide.md`](../../docs/contributor-guide.md) **Commit Style**. Squash-merge: [`.cursor/skills/squash-commit-message/SKILL.md`](../../.cursor/skills/squash-commit-message/SKILL.md).

## Title (subject line)

- Lower-case first character
- One concise line; no `docs:` / `feat:` prefixes
- No issue references in PR titles

## Body

- **Never** start the body with an upper-case letter (first line and every bullet)
- **Do not** write the body as sentences or paragraphs
- Use short phrase-style lines (clauses), not full sentences with a trailing period habit
- **Two or more** logical items: markdown bullets (`- `), each starting lower-case
- **Exactly one** logical item: a single lower-case line with no bullet is OK
- **Do not** use upper-case to start bullets for emphasis (`- Add tests` is wrong; `- add tests` is right)

## Bad vs good

Bad (prose paragraph):

```
rename foo to bar

Align the skill and AGENTS.md with the new heading used on the issue.
```

Good (bullets):

```
rename foo to bar

- align skill and AGENTS.md with issue comment heading
```

Good (single item, one lower-case line, no bullet):

```
fix off-by-one in combat tick

correct bandit reply index when handover is active
```

## Squash-merge

Same body rules; title often ends with `(#<pr>)`. See squash-commit-message skill.
